' Capability vs Agentic Capability 2x2 matrix
'
' Per ADR-ES-012 §14.
' Illustrates the Agentic / Autonomous orthogonality at the
' capability boundary.
'
' Authored by: Emmanuel A. Otchere (cardinal author rule, 2026-09-24)

@startuml capability-vs-agentic-capability

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title Capability 2x2 Matrix: Agentic vs Autonomous

' 2x2 matrix

rectangle "Capability\n(universal, ADR-ES-002)" as base #E6E6FA

rectangle "Conventional\n(no agentic, no autonomous)" as cv #FFFFFF

rectangle "Agentic Capability\n(ADR-ES-012, established)" as ac #FFE4B5

rectangle "Autonomous Capability\n(ADR-ES-013, deferred)" as auc #E0FFE0

rectangle "Agentic + Autonomous\n(orthogonal combination, possible)" as combo #F0F8FF

base --> cv
base --> ac
base --> auc
base --> combo

note bottom
  Per ADR-ES-012 §14: only Agentic Capability is established
  by ADR-ES-012. Autonomous Capability remains deferred per
  ADR-ES-012 §25. The 2x2 matrix permits Autonomous Capability
  as a future orthogonal specialization (ADR-ES-013).
end note

@enduml
